  "id": "COMPOUND:16211 - PROTEIN:1106",
  "verbalization": "Paeonilide appears to interact with the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2 through a series of target relationships, all mediated by the T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 zeta chain. This pathway suggests that Paeonilide acts as a ligand or modulator of the GABA receptor subunit gamma-2, potentially influencing GABAergic signaling in cellular processes. The evidence is supported by multiple high-scoring connections, indicating a consistent and robust relationship across different compounds. The shared involvement of the CD3 zeta chain as a target suggests a common mechanism or pathway, possibly related to immune or cellular signaling functions. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of Paeonilide in modulating GABA receptor activity, which may have implications for therapeutic applications targeting GABAergic systems.",
